==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=normality}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|normal|ity|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ælɪti|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|normalities}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The state of being [[normal]] or [[usual]]; [[normalcy]].
#: ''Jessie was going to wear pants to school, but her brother persuaded her to wear shorts to preserve '''normality'''.''
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} The [[concentration]] of a [[solution]] expressed in [[gram equivalent weight]]s of [[solute]] per [[litre]] of [[solution]].
# {{lb|en|countable|mathematics|statistics}} A [[measure]] of how well an observed [[distribution]] approximates a [[normal distribution]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|state of being normal}} {{l|en|normalcy}} {{qualifier|US}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|abnormality}}

